@startuml subtask_policies
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' subtask_policies — the v28.3 feature in one picture: ONE piece, and the
' five query policies that project it differently ON PURPOSE.
'
' Read it left to right: the flat m_tasks vector holds a parent and its
' piece (the link is parentId, pointing UP); each query on the right
' answers a DIFFERENT question, so each treats the piece differently —
' the design's whole point (design-addendum-subtasks.md §D). The dashed
' box at the bottom is what never happens: completion roll-up.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

skinparam rectangleFontSize 12

rectangle "**AppData::m_tasks**  (one flat vector)" as store {
  rectangle "**Lab 4**\n(parent · due Aug 8\nestimate 120 min)" as parent #E8F0EC
  rectangle "**Marc's section**\n(piece · due Aug 4\nestimate 25 min)" as piece #FFFFFF
}
piece -up-> parent : parentId\n(one level,\ndoor-enforced)

rectangle "**upcomingTasks() / tasksIn()**\n« workload — parents only »\nshows: Lab 4" as workload #E8F0EC
rectangle "**tasksDueOn(Aug 4)**\n« that day's obligations »\nshows: Marc's section" as dueon #E8F0EC
rectangle "**taskCountIn(School)**\n« the deletion guard »\ncounts: 2 (everything)" as guard #FDF3F2
rectangle "**pieceProgress(Lab 4)**\n« the card's ☑ chip »\nanswers: 0 / 1" as chip #E8F0EC

parent --> workload
piece -[#C25B54,dashed]-> workload : filtered out\n(double-counts\nthe parent)
piece --> dueon : dated → a real\nobligation that day
parent --> guard
piece --> guard : counted —\nundercounting\ndeletes data
piece --> chip

rectangle "**what never happens**\nticking every piece does NOT complete the parent —\nthe tick is the reward, in both directions" as rollup #FFFFFF
parent -[#616974,dotted]- rollup

legend bottom
  One fact, five truthful projections: the queries **disagree on purpose**
  because they answer different questions. Archive cascades both directions;
  delete cascades with title-demotion; spawn keeps parentId + size.
endlegend
@enduml
